{"name":"Sleep","hex":"#4579ac","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sleep","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sleep"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sleep","blocks":[{"text":"Sleep is a state of reduced mental and physical activity in which consciousness is altered and certain sensory activity is inhibited. During sleep, there is a marked decrease in muscle activity and interactions with the surrounding environment. While sleep differs from wakefulness in terms of the ability to react to stimuli, it still involves active brain patterns, making it more reactive than a coma or disorders of consciousness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg/330px-Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sleep"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/1900_The_Awakening.jpg/500px-1900_The_Awakening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/1900_The_Awakening.jpg/500px-1900_The_Awakening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"The Awakening\", an illustration to writing by Leo Tolstoy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1900_The_Awakening.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png/250px-Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/33/Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Pillow